+<h2>84. isPlatformRole and requireKeyAdmin compare the role as an exact ASCII fold and refuse a role that is not a string (KS-1591)</h2>
+<table class="pmatrix"><tr><td class="pm-topic" rowspan="2"><strong>What this changes.</strong></td><td> KS-1591 (a security nit, pre-existing): two predicates decided &ldquo;platform administrator&rdquo; and &ldquo;key administrator&rdquo; with <code>String(role).toUpperCase()</code>, which is not an identity test. U+0131 (dotless i) upper-cases to <code>I</code>, U+017F (long s) upper-cases to <code>S</code>, and a role ARRAY stringifies to its element, so a role spelled with either character, or an array holding <code>SUPER_ADMIN</code>, read as an admin role. <code>isPlatformRole</code> in <code>packages/shared/src/security/keyRevokePolicy.ts</code> and <code>requireKeyAdmin</code> in <code>services/security/src/index.ts</code> now apply an ASCII fold only (a-z to A-Z, every other character untouched) and treat a role that is not a string as no role. Every ASCII spelling admitted before is admitted now. Two local-model passes (the Spark, DeepSeek V4 Flash: <code>ks_1591_p1</code> and <code>ks_1591_p2_security</code>) each passed their checker 7 of 7 and are byte-identical to the drafter&rsquo;s golden; both were applied here strictly and unchanged. </td></tr><tr><td>In each product file one line is replaced by four (+4 / &minus;1). Two test files are added: <code>packages/shared/src/__tests__/ks1591-is-platform-role-is-an-exact-ascii-fold.test.ts</code> (vitest, 13 cells) and <code>services/security/src/__tests__/ks1591-require-key-admin-is-an-exact-ascii-fold.test.ts</code> (vitest, 7 cells; it boots the real app over HTTP with an RS256 token). The change fails toward LESS access. No tier timing or budget in these documents moves.
+    </td></tr></table>
+<h3>84.1 Red-first, and the figures</h3>
