+</table>
+<h3>84.2 What the cells prove, and what they do not</h3>
+<table class="pmatrix"><tr><td class="pm-topic" rowspan="2"><strong>The two predicates, not their callers.</strong></td><td> The shared cells pin that U+0131, U+017F and a role array are refused by <code>isPlatformRole</code>, that every ASCII spelling the platform uses is still admitted, that an ordinary, an empty and an absent role are still refused, and (D1, D2) that <code>decideTenantAccess</code>, the caller, sees the refusal. The security cells pin the same three refusals at the HTTP edge of <code>GET /api/keys</code>, and that no token is still 401, ISSUER_ADMIN in three casings is 200 and USER is 403. Cell R3 of the security test accepts a 401 or a 403 for an array role: it asserts refusal, not which layer refuses. </td></tr><tr><td>Not measured: whether such a role can reach either predicate in production (the ticket says reachability is not established), the other importers of <code>isPlatformRole</code> (originate and others; their suites were not run), a running stack, the four platform suites (Schemathesis, Akto, Playwright, Performance/k6), a Node 24 LTS run, and any deploy. None of them is claimed as passing.
